select 'pv-drone-1', 'problem-drone-dynamics', 1, 'Drone Dynamics Adaptation', 'A controller succeeds in simulation and fails in flight. Design a learning signal for an adaptive representation.', 'A drone controller performs well in simulation but becomes unstable after deployment. Motor strength, payload, mass, and aerodynamic characteristics differ from the simulator. An encoder observes a recent window of states and actions, produces a latent vector z, and passes it to the controller alongside the current state. You can change the encoder''s training objective.', 'How should the representation be trained so that the latent captures information useful for adapting to the drone''s real dynamics? Explain your learning signal, what information it encourages z to retain, and how you would check that it works.', array['State estimates and executed actions are available; true physical parameters are not available on the real drone.', 'Simulation can generate trajectories under a range of physical parameters. Dynamics are approximately constant within a short history window.', 'The controller can consume the latent vector. Sensor latency and hardware faults have been ruled out for this scenario.']::text[], '{"kind":"flow","title":"The adaptation loop","caption":"The history provides context; the current state also enters the controller. The encoder''s learning signal is your design decision.","nodes":[{"id":"history","label":"Recent history","detail":"states + actions"},{"id":"encoder","label":"Encoder","detail":"history → context"},{"id":"latent","label":"Latent z","detail":"compact context"},{"id":"controller","label":"Controller","detail":"+ current state"},{"id":"action","label":"Action","detail":"motor commands"}]}'::jsonb, 'applied', array['objective_design', 'experiment_design']::text[], 'intermediate', array['Adaptation', 'Control', 'Representation']::text[], 'original_mock'
